{"kind":"assert","text":"P1 source plan 64bc7afd with precision ae9e41e6: accepted, with three\nchanges. Rulings 36915a7c and the Git ruling beside this act answer\nthe two questions that the plan leaves open.\n\n1. Layout. Each new P1 source file lives in\n   `examples/lending/publisher/`: the definition, its JSON and pin\n   when a consumer needs them, the role table, the map, the fold, the\n   publisher, the Git port, the two scripts and the test file. Name\n   the files without the `publisher-` prefix there.\n2. Shared files. P1 changes no file that `dap pack` reads for the\n   shipped Lending package. The edit of `test-support.ts` and the\n   edit of the example's Vitest and TypeScript includes stay\n   permitted. When `dap pack` reads one of those files, stop and ask.\n3. Names. The definition name `lending-publisher` is accepted. The\n   package name is `ai.generalbusiness.lending.publisher`, as ruled.\n\nAccepted as planned:\n\n- The commit of a publication has one exact parent and a time taken\n  from the `through` entry. The reader and the publisher share one\n  fold and one byte construction.\n- A read that is refused, filtered or incomplete stops the cycle\n  with no signature and no push.\n- Witnesses 2 and 3 use new Node child processes, a bare repository\n  and file custody. The parent answers the children over IPC.\n- Witness 3 uses two keys of one appointed member. State in the note\n  that the membership rows are scripted.\n\nOne more case for witness 3, in the same test or the note: two\nprocesses that hold the same key and sign the same report. State\nwhat the scope answers to the second one. When the answer is the\nfirst receipt, that is correct, and the note says so.\n\nStart the source now. Run nothing while the CUT-A follow-up holds the\nexecutable slot.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}